<title>CANADA: Copper concentrate ship runs aground in Canada.</title>
<headline>Copper concentrate ship runs aground in Canada.</headline>
<dateline>TORONTO 1996-12-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>A ship carrying up to 25,000 tonnes of Chilean copper concentrate has run aground in the Gulf of St. Lawrence offshore Quebec, a spokesman for Noranda Inc said on Monday.</p>
<p>The ship was carrying copper concentrate from the Escondida mine in Chile, owned by Broken Hill Proprietary Co Ltd, and was headed to Noranda's copper smelter in Gaspe, Quebec, Gilles Gratton said in an interview. The incident will have no impact on Noranda's production, he said.</p>
<p>The ship got stuck on a sandbar on the weekend, he said.</p>
<p>&quot;They tried to remove the boat on its own power on the weekend, but it didn't work,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>He said he expects the ship to be removed sometime this week.</p>
<p>((Reuters Toronto Bureau 416 941-8100))</p>
